OL,3,GNEWSAFears for my son's safety in
OL,4,Amainstream school keep me awake at
OL,5,Anight
OL,6,
OL,7,FFreddie has no sense of danger and eats
OL,8,Fnon-edible objects. He bangs his head
OL,9,Fand climbs. His mum, Natalie, says she
OL,10,Fneeds eyes in the back of her head.
OL,12,FBut there is no place at special school
OL,13,Ffor him so the four-year-old from Essex
OL,14,Fwill start in mainstream education in
OL,15,FSeptember.
OL,17,FNatalie says the thought of this is
OL,18,F"keeping her awake at night" but the
OL,19,Ffamily must wait until 2028 to appeal
OL,20,Fagainst the decision.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
